WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.720
A square of dots grows from three rows of three to four

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.610
rows of four.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.990
How many dots are added?

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.640
And what is the rule for growing any square to

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.370
the next one?

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.600
Keep the nine original dots.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.520
Add a new bottom row.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.920
The new row belongs to the bigger square,

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.500
so it has four dots.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.490
Now add the new right-hand column.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.450
Its bottom dot is already there, as part of the new row.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.850
So only three more dots are needed.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.180
Four plus three is seven dots added.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:37.220
Nine plus seven is sixteen, which is four times four.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.970
The same picture works for any size.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.050
To grow a square of side n, add a row of n plus one dots

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.630
and a column of n dots.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.230
That is two n plus one dots.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.500
So from ten by ten to eleven by eleven you

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.750
add twenty-one dots.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.640
That is why the gaps between square numbers are the odd

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.770
numbers: three, five, seven, nine.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.740
Rebuild this argument, then answer: how many dots are

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.300
added when a twenty by twenty square grows to

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.730
twenty-one by twenty-one?
